=== Lab task 4: fleet-tracked shipping container across an ocean ===
Distance to the nearest terrestrial base station in mid-ocean is hundreds of km; with the
same model PL(500 km) = 186.0 dB, far beyond every MCL above (max 152 dB):
the link-budget sum is not merely 'tight' - there is no terrestrial network to budget against.
The decision hinges on non-radio axes: satellite/NTN availability, roaming agreements,
store-and-forward at ports, device cost and mobility - not on a single-distance margin.

Technologies meeting BOTH margin>0 and >=5 years: NB-IoT, LoRaWAN
Qualitative axes (Section 4.3): no cellular coverage nearby -> NB-IoT / LTE-M need an operator network
that does not exist on this farm; LoRaWAN needs only 1-2 self-owned gateways, no per-device fee.
RECOMMENDATION: LoRaWAN (SF12) with 1-2 farm-owned gateways.
